-- ============================================================================
-- DC12 - Earth Modeling Beginner (Associate) goes deep.
--
-- Flips (earthmodel, beginner) onto the DC1 deep path by inserting its ACTIVE
-- academy_course_structures row, generated from the repo manifest
-- src/content/courses/earthmodel/beginner/manifest.json (the structure source
-- of truth; this file was emitted by a generator, not hand-typed), and
-- seeding the module quiz banks (15+15+15+15+15+15 questions) plus the
-- 42-question final exam bank. Answer keys live only here and in the
-- table (no client SELECT policies); the repo lesson content carries no
-- graded questions.
--
-- Every numeric question traces to the earthmodel teaching oracle and
-- reproduces the live NG10 Beginner capstone answer key: three source
-- surfaces on three DIFFERENT grids resampled onto the 25x20 / 50 m
-- model frame, clamped depth-down, then differenced into zones (mean
-- TopB 1575.5 m, 180 BaseB nodes fixed by the clamp, zone A mean 36 m
-- and max 42 m, zone B mean 10.24 m, zone A bulk 45e6 m3 as a
-- closed-form anchor). The golden model carries a dual stdlib-Python
-- oracle. That is the same pipeline src/lib/earthmodelTeaching.js
-- drives and src/components/course/panels/earthmodel/
-- frameworkLab.test.js pins.
--
-- Scope note (binding, from the G8 plan): this course owns the
-- container. Fluids, contacts and STOIIP booking stay in the
-- ReservoirCalc course, and the bulk rock volume is the hand-off.
--
-- Enrollment grandfathering: enforced_from defaults to now() on first
-- insert, so learners enrolled before this apply finish on the old path;
-- the ON CONFLICT update deliberately leaves enforced_from unchanged on
-- re-seeds. Re-seeding replaces the whole bank for this course-tier;
-- fine while there are no open attempts (open attempts pin question ids).
-- ============================================================================

values ('earthmodel', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-what-an-earth-model-is","title":"What an Earth Model Is","lesson_keys":["l01-why-build-a-model","l02-the-container-not-the-barrels","l03-the-golden-model","l04-the-beginner-framework-map"]},{"key":"m02-one-frame-many-grids","title":"One Frame, Many Grids","lesson_keys":["l01-surfaces-arrive-on-their-own-grids","l02-the-model-frame","l03-resampling","l04-what-resampling-cannot-fix"]},{"key":"m03-the-depth-down-clamp","title":"The Depth-Down Clamp","lesson_keys":["l01-a-model-must-be-valid","l02-the-monotonic-clamp","l03-the-180-fixed-nodes","l04-a-clamp-count-is-information"]},{"key":"m04-zones-and-thickness","title":"Zones and Thickness","lesson_keys":["l01-from-surfaces-to-zones","l02-zone-a","l03-zone-b-pinches-out","l04-means-over-what","l05-reading-a-thickness-map"]},{"key":"m05-bulk-rock-volume","title":"Bulk Rock Volume","lesson_keys":["l01-what-bulk-volume-is","l02-the-closed-form-check","l03-zone-b-volume","l04-where-the-volume-goes-next"]},{"key":"m06-the-earth-modeling-workflow","title":"The Earth Modeling Workflow","lesson_keys":["l01-the-workflow-end-to-end","l02-quality-control","l03-the-capstone-walkthrough","l04-onward-to-professional"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
